window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/a074-92ab2a1822ea2e63.json"]={sha256:"92ab2a1822ea2e6338f0aebeb6c8ab717116af86223765bb22bffc8bfcfc3967",value:{"id":"a074","title":"相變化記憶體製作","titleEn":"Phase-change memory fabrication","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process","v8-c-imec-place","v8-c-nanoic-open","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從相態與電阻、脈衝能量到陣列耐久度：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Phase and resistance and Pulse energy to Array endurance: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["相態與電阻","熱阻網路","受限相變體積","選擇器與偷流"],"labelsEn":["Phase and resistance","Thermal network","Confined active volume","Selector and sneak paths"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a074-stage01","order":1,"title":"相態與電阻 → 加熱器幾何","titleEn":"Phase and resistance to Heater geometry","description":"把「相態與電阻」「SET 與 RESET」「加熱器幾何」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Phase and resistance, SET and RESET, Heater geometry.","steps":[{"id":"a074-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"相態與電阻：建立模型","titleEn":"Phase and resistance: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「電阻對比來自材料狀態而非永久斷路」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Resistance contrast reflects material state, not necessarily permanent rupture.","instruction":"畫晶態及非晶態原子示意，連結到兩組假設電阻分布。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Sketch crystalline/amorphous arrangements and connect them to resistance distributions. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"電阻對比來自材料狀態而非永久斷路；電阻讀取應避免再次加熱改態。","observationEn":"Resistance contrast reflects material state, not necessarily permanent rupture; Read bias should avoid reheating the state.","failure":"若採用「把高阻態都視為燒斷導線」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating every high-resistance state as a burnt wire\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「相態與電阻」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：電阻對比來自材料狀態而非永久斷路。","checkEn":"Submit the Phase and resistance diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Resistance contrast reflects material state, not necessarily permanent rupture.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-01-k1","title":"相態與電阻／物理與模型","titleEn":"Phase and resistance / Physics and model","text":"機制：電阻對比來自材料狀態而非永久斷路。","textEn":"Mechanism: Resistance contrast reflects material state, not necessarily permanent rupture."},{"id":"a074-v8-01-k2","title":"相態與電阻／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Phase and resistance / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把高阻態都視為燒斷導線」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating every high-resistance state as a burnt wire."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「相態與電阻」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Phase and resistance, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["電阻對比來自材料狀態而非永久斷路","把高阻態都視為燒斷導線","只比較最大脈衝幅度判斷最終相態"],"optionsEn":["Resistance contrast reflects material state, not necessarily permanent rupture","Treating every high-resistance state as a burnt wire","Judging final phase from maximum pulse amplitude alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"電阻對比來自材料狀態而非永久斷路；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Resistance contrast reflects material state, not necessarily permanent rupture. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-01"],"title":"相態與電阻：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Phase and resistance: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把高阻態都視為燒斷導線」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating every high-resistance state as a burnt wire.","instruction":"接續前一步「相態與電阻」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把高阻態都視為燒斷導線」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：電阻讀取應避免再次加熱改態。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Phase and resistance artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating every high-resistance state as a burnt wire\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Read bias should avoid reheating the state. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"電阻對比來自材料狀態而非永久斷路；電阻讀取應避免再次加熱改態。","observationEn":"Resistance contrast reflects material state, not necessarily permanent rupture; Read bias should avoid reheating the state.","failure":"若採用「把高阻態都視為燒斷導線」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating every high-resistance state as a burnt wire\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「相態與電阻」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「電阻讀取應避免再次加熱改態」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Phase and resistance, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Read bias should avoid reheating the state\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-02-k1","title":"相態與電阻／物理與模型","titleEn":"Phase and resistance / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：電阻讀取應避免再次加熱改態。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Read bias should avoid reheating the state."},{"id":"a074-v8-02-k2","title":"相態與電阻／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Phase and resistance / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把高阻態都視為燒斷導線」與「電阻對比來自材料狀態而非永久斷路」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating every high-resistance state as a burnt wire\" is not equivalent to \"Resistance contrast reflects material state, not necessarily permanent rupture\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「相態與電阻」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Phase and resistance?","options":["只比較最大脈衝幅度判斷最終相態","電阻讀取應避免再次加熱改態","把高阻態都視為燒斷導線"],"optionsEn":["Judging final phase from maximum pulse amplitude alone","Read bias should avoid reheating the state","Treating every high-resistance state as a burnt wire"],"answer":1,"explanation":"電阻讀取應避免再次加熱改態；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Read bias should avoid reheating the state. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-02"],"title":"SET 與 RESET：建立模型","titleEn":"SET and RESET: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「峰值溫度與冷卻歷史共同決定相態」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Peak temperature and cooling history jointly determine phase.","instruction":"畫結晶保溫與熔融後快冷的概念溫度時間曲線。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw conceptual crystallizing dwell and melt-quench temperature trajectories. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"峰值溫度與冷卻歷史共同決定相態；冷卻速率會影響非晶化。","observationEn":"Peak temperature and cooling history jointly determine phase; Cooling rate affects amorphization.","failure":"若採用「只比較最大脈衝幅度判斷最終相態」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Judging final phase from maximum pulse amplitude alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「SET 與 RESET」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：峰值溫度與冷卻歷史共同決定相態。","checkEn":"Submit the SET and RESET diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Peak temperature and cooling history jointly determine phase.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-03-k1","title":"SET 與 RESET／物理與模型","titleEn":"SET and RESET / Physics and model","text":"機制：峰值溫度與冷卻歷史共同決定相態。","textEn":"Mechanism: Peak temperature and cooling history jointly determine phase."},{"id":"a074-v8-03-k2","title":"SET 與 RESET／驗證與限制","titleEn":"SET and RESET / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只比較最大脈衝幅度判斷最終相態」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Judging final phase from maximum pulse amplitude alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「SET 與 RESET」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For SET and RESET, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只比較最大脈衝幅度判斷最終相態","只以整顆元件體積計算切換能量","峰值溫度與冷卻歷史共同決定相態"],"optionsEn":["Judging final phase from maximum pulse amplitude alone","Estimating switching energy from total device volume alone","Peak temperature and cooling history jointly determine phase"],"answer":2,"explanation":"峰值溫度與冷卻歷史共同決定相態；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Peak temperature and cooling history jointly determine phase. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-03"],"title":"SET 與 RESET：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"SET and RESET: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只比較最大脈衝幅度判斷最終相態」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Judging final phase from maximum pulse amplitude alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「SET 與 RESET」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只比較最大脈衝幅度判斷最終相態」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：冷卻速率會影響非晶化。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding SET and RESET artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Judging final phase from maximum pulse amplitude alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Cooling rate affects amorphization. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"峰值溫度與冷卻歷史共同決定相態；冷卻速率會影響非晶化。","observationEn":"Peak temperature and cooling history jointly determine phase; Cooling rate affects amorphization.","failure":"若採用「只比較最大脈衝幅度判斷最終相態」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Judging final phase from maximum pulse amplitude alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「SET 與 RESET」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「冷卻速率會影響非晶化」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for SET and RESET, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Cooling rate affects amorphization\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-04-k1","title":"SET 與 RESET／物理與模型","titleEn":"SET and RESET / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：冷卻速率會影響非晶化。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Cooling rate affects amorphization."},{"id":"a074-v8-04-k2","title":"SET 與 RESET／驗證與限制","titleEn":"SET and RESET / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只比較最大脈衝幅度判斷最終相態」與「峰值溫度與冷卻歷史共同決定相態」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Judging final phase from maximum pulse amplitude alone\" is not equivalent to \"Peak temperature and cooling history jointly determine phase\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「SET 與 RESET」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of SET and RESET?","options":["冷卻速率會影響非晶化","只比較最大脈衝幅度判斷最終相態","只以整顆元件體積計算切換能量"],"optionsEn":["Cooling rate affects amorphization","Judging final phase from maximum pulse amplitude alone","Estimating switching energy from total device volume alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"冷卻速率會影響非晶化；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Cooling rate affects amorphization. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-04"],"title":"加熱器幾何：建立模型","titleEn":"Heater geometry: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「加熱效率與有效相變體積相關」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Heating efficiency relates to active phase-change volume.","instruction":"比較小接觸與大接觸的熱集中位置並標示電流路徑。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare heat localization for small/large contacts and mark current paths. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"加熱效率與有效相變體積相關；接觸電阻也影響局部發熱。","observationEn":"Heating efficiency relates to active phase-change volume; Contact resistance changes local heating.","failure":"若採用「只以整顆元件體積計算切換能量」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Estimating switching energy from total device volume alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「加熱器幾何」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：加熱效率與有效相變體積相關。","checkEn":"Submit the Heater geometry diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Heating efficiency relates to active phase-change volume.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-05-k1","title":"加熱器幾何／物理與模型","titleEn":"Heater geometry / Physics and model","text":"機制：加熱效率與有效相變體積相關。","textEn":"Mechanism: Heating efficiency relates to active phase-change volume."},{"id":"a074-v8-05-k2","title":"加熱器幾何／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Heater geometry / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只以整顆元件體積計算切換能量」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Estimating switching energy from total device volume alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「加熱器幾何」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Heater geometry, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["熱阻越高就保證 RESET 越容易","加熱效率與有效相變體積相關","只以整顆元件體積計算切換能量"],"optionsEn":["Assuming higher thermal resistance always simplifies RESET","Heating efficiency relates to active phase-change volume","Estimating switching energy from total device volume alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"加熱效率與有效相變體積相關；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Heating efficiency relates to active phase-change volume. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-05"],"title":"加熱器幾何：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Heater geometry: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只以整顆元件體積計算切換能量」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Estimating switching energy from total device volume alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「加熱器幾何」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只以整顆元件體積計算切換能量」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：接觸電阻也影響局部發熱。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Heater geometry artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Estimating switching energy from total device volume alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Contact resistance changes local heating. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"加熱效率與有效相變體積相關；接觸電阻也影響局部發熱。","observationEn":"Heating efficiency relates to active phase-change volume; Contact resistance changes local heating.","failure":"若採用「只以整顆元件體積計算切換能量」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Estimating switching energy from total device volume alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「加熱器幾何」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「接觸電阻也影響局部發熱」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Heater geometry, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Contact resistance changes local heating\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-06-k1","title":"加熱器幾何／物理與模型","titleEn":"Heater geometry / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：接觸電阻也影響局部發熱。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Contact resistance changes local heating."},{"id":"a074-v8-06-k2","title":"加熱器幾何／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Heater geometry / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只以整顆元件體積計算切換能量」與「加熱效率與有效相變體積相關」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Estimating switching energy from total device volume alone\" is not equivalent to \"Heating efficiency relates to active phase-change volume\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「加熱器幾何」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Heater geometry?","options":["只以整顆元件體積計算切換能量","熱阻越高就保證 RESET 越容易","接觸電阻也影響局部發熱"],"optionsEn":["Estimating switching energy from total device volume alone","Assuming higher thermal resistance always simplifies RESET","Contact resistance changes local heating"],"answer":2,"explanation":"接觸電阻也影響局部發熱；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Contact resistance changes local heating. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a074-stage02","order":2,"title":"熱阻網路 → 材料組成","titleEn":"Thermal network to Material composition","description":"把「熱阻網路」「脈衝能量」「材料組成」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Thermal network, Pulse energy, Material composition.","steps":[{"id":"a074-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-06"],"title":"熱阻網路：建立模型","titleEn":"Thermal network: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「熱侷限有助加熱但也影響冷卻」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Thermal confinement aids heating but also affects cooling.","instruction":"畫相變層到電極及基板的熱阻，計算假設穩態溫升。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw thermal paths to electrodes/substrate and estimate hypothetical steady rise. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"熱侷限有助加熱但也影響冷卻；多條熱路徑需要並聯組合。","observationEn":"Thermal confinement aids heating but also affects cooling; Multiple thermal paths combine in parallel.","failure":"若採用「熱阻越高就保證 RESET 越容易」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming higher thermal resistance always simplifies RESET\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「熱阻網路」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：熱侷限有助加熱但也影響冷卻。","checkEn":"Submit the Thermal network diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Thermal confinement aids heating but also affects cooling.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-07-k1","title":"熱阻網路／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thermal network / Physics and model","text":"機制：熱侷限有助加熱但也影響冷卻。","textEn":"Mechanism: Thermal confinement aids heating but also affects cooling."},{"id":"a074-v8-07-k2","title":"熱阻網路／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thermal network / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「熱阻越高就保證 RESET 越容易」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming higher thermal resistance always simplifies RESET."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「熱阻網路」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Thermal network, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["熱侷限有助加熱但也影響冷卻","熱阻越高就保證 RESET 越容易","相同焦耳數就必有相同材料狀態"],"optionsEn":["Thermal confinement aids heating but also affects cooling","Assuming higher thermal resistance always simplifies RESET","Equating joules with identical material states"],"answer":0,"explanation":"熱侷限有助加熱但也影響冷卻；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Thermal confinement aids heating but also affects cooling. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-07"],"title":"熱阻網路：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Thermal network: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「熱阻越高就保證 RESET 越容易」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming higher thermal resistance always simplifies RESET.","instruction":"接續前一步「熱阻網路」成果，先指出錯誤主張「熱阻越高就保證 RESET 越容易」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：多條熱路徑需要並聯組合。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Thermal network artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming higher thermal resistance always simplifies RESET\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Multiple thermal paths combine in parallel. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"熱侷限有助加熱但也影響冷卻；多條熱路徑需要並聯組合。","observationEn":"Thermal confinement aids heating but also affects cooling; Multiple thermal paths combine in parallel.","failure":"若採用「熱阻越高就保證 RESET 越容易」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming higher thermal resistance always simplifies RESET\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「熱阻網路」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「多條熱路徑需要並聯組合」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Thermal network, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Multiple thermal paths combine in parallel\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-08-k1","title":"熱阻網路／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thermal network / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：多條熱路徑需要並聯組合。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Multiple thermal paths combine in parallel."},{"id":"a074-v8-08-k2","title":"熱阻網路／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thermal network / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「熱阻越高就保證 RESET 越容易」與「熱侷限有助加熱但也影響冷卻」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming higher thermal resistance always simplifies RESET\" is not equivalent to \"Thermal confinement aids heating but also affects cooling\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「熱阻網路」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Thermal network?","options":["相同焦耳數就必有相同材料狀態","多條熱路徑需要並聯組合","熱阻越高就保證 RESET 越容易"],"optionsEn":["Equating joules with identical material states","Multiple thermal paths combine in parallel","Assuming higher thermal resistance always simplifies RESET"],"answer":1,"explanation":"多條熱路徑需要並聯組合；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Multiple thermal paths combine in parallel. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-08"],"title":"脈衝能量：建立模型","titleEn":"Pulse energy: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「相同能量不同時間形狀可形成不同溫度軌跡」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Equal energies with different shapes can yield different thermal histories.","instruction":"對假設 V(t)、I(t) 做能量積分，分辨峰值功率與總能量。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設在 PCM 元件端量到理想矩形脈衝，V=2 V、I=0.5 mA、持續 20 ns，電能 E=VIt=20 pJ。保持 V、I 不變而時間加倍，電能為 40 pJ。這不等於材料吸收熱量，亦不能證明 RESET；熱損失、脈衝邊緣及動態電阻另需量測。","instructionEn":"Integrate hypothetical V(t)I(t) and distinguish peak power from total energy. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume an ideal rectangular pulse measured at a PCM device: V=2 V, I=0.5 mA for 20 ns. Electrical energy E=VIt=20 pJ; doubling duration at fixed V and I gives 40 pJ. This is not absorbed material heat and does not prove RESET; thermal loss, pulse edges and dynamic resistance need separate evidence.","observation":"相同能量不同時間形狀可形成不同溫度軌跡；波形線纜損失會改變晶片實際脈衝。","observationEn":"Equal energies with different shapes can yield different thermal histories; Cable loss changes the actual die pulse.","failure":"若採用「相同焦耳數就必有相同材料狀態」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating joules with identical material states\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「脈衝能量」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：相同能量不同時間形狀可形成不同溫度軌跡。\n算例驗收：以瓦特與秒核對 20 pJ，區分電能、溫度與相態三個不同量。","checkEn":"Submit the Pulse energy diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Equal energies with different shapes can yield different thermal histories.\nWorked-example acceptance: Check 20 pJ using watts and seconds and distinguish electrical energy, temperature and phase.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-09-k1","title":"脈衝能量／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pulse energy / Physics and model","text":"機制：相同能量不同時間形狀可形成不同溫度軌跡。","textEn":"Mechanism: Equal energies with different shapes can yield different thermal histories."},{"id":"a074-v8-09-k2","title":"脈衝能量／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pulse energy / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「相同焦耳數就必有相同材料狀態」。\n假設數值與推算：假設在 PCM 元件端量到理想矩形脈衝，V=2 V、I=0.5 mA、持續 20 ns，電能 E=VIt=20 pJ。保持 V、I 不變而時間加倍，電能為 40 pJ。這不等於材料吸收熱量，亦不能證明 RESET；熱損失、脈衝邊緣及動態電阻另需量測。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating joules with identical material states.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume an ideal rectangular pulse measured at a PCM device: V=2 V, I=0.5 mA for 20 ns. Electrical energy E=VIt=20 pJ; doubling duration at fixed V and I gives 40 pJ. This is not absorbed material heat and does not prove RESET; thermal loss, pulse edges and dynamic resistance need separate evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「脈衝能量」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Pulse energy, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["相同焦耳數就必有相同材料狀態","只追求最快結晶而忽略非晶保持","相同能量不同時間形狀可形成不同溫度軌跡"],"optionsEn":["Equating joules with identical material states","Optimizing crystallization speed while ignoring amorphous retention","Equal energies with different shapes can yield different thermal histories"],"answer":2,"explanation":"相同能量不同時間形狀可形成不同溫度軌跡；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Equal energies with different shapes can yield different thermal histories. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-09"],"title":"脈衝能量：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Pulse energy: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「相同焦耳數就必有相同材料狀態」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating joules with identical material states.","instruction":"接續前一步「脈衝能量」成果，先指出錯誤主張「相同焦耳數就必有相同材料狀態」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：波形線纜損失會改變晶片實際脈衝。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Pulse energy artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating joules with identical material states\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Cable loss changes the actual die pulse. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"相同能量不同時間形狀可形成不同溫度軌跡；波形線纜損失會改變晶片實際脈衝。","observationEn":"Equal energies with different shapes can yield different thermal histories; Cable loss changes the actual die pulse.","failure":"若採用「相同焦耳數就必有相同材料狀態」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating joules with identical material states\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「脈衝能量」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「波形線纜損失會改變晶片實際脈衝」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Pulse energy, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Cable loss changes the actual die pulse\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-10-k1","title":"脈衝能量／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pulse energy / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：波形線纜損失會改變晶片實際脈衝。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Cable loss changes the actual die pulse."},{"id":"a074-v8-10-k2","title":"脈衝能量／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pulse energy / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「相同焦耳數就必有相同材料狀態」與「相同能量不同時間形狀可形成不同溫度軌跡」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating joules with identical material states\" is not equivalent to \"Equal energies with different shapes can yield different thermal histories\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「脈衝能量」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Pulse energy?","options":["波形線纜損失會改變晶片實際脈衝","相同焦耳數就必有相同材料狀態","只追求最快結晶而忽略非晶保持"],"optionsEn":["Cable loss changes the actual die pulse","Equating joules with identical material states","Optimizing crystallization speed while ignoring amorphous retention"],"answer":0,"explanation":"波形線纜損失會改變晶片實際脈衝；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Cable loss changes the actual die pulse. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-10"],"title":"材料組成：建立模型","titleEn":"Material composition: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「材料選擇同時受切換與穩定性約束」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Materials are constrained by switching and stability together.","instruction":"比較兩種假設組成的結晶速度、保持與漂移需求表。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare hypothetical compositions for crystallization speed, retention and drift. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"材料選擇同時受切換與穩定性約束；材料偏析可能累積造成失效。","observationEn":"Materials are constrained by switching and stability together; Segregation can accumulate into failure.","failure":"若採用「只追求最快結晶而忽略非晶保持」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Optimizing crystallization speed while ignoring amorphous retention\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「材料組成」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：材料選擇同時受切換與穩定性約束。","checkEn":"Submit the Material composition diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Materials are constrained by switching and stability together.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-11-k1","title":"材料組成／物理與模型","titleEn":"Material composition / Physics and model","text":"機制：材料選擇同時受切換與穩定性約束。","textEn":"Mechanism: Materials are constrained by switching and stability together."},{"id":"a074-v8-11-k2","title":"材料組成／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Material composition / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只追求最快結晶而忽略非晶保持」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Optimizing crystallization speed while ignoring amorphous retention."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「材料組成」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Material composition, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把全部沉積材料當成每次都重熔","材料選擇同時受切換與穩定性約束","只追求最快結晶而忽略非晶保持"],"optionsEn":["Assuming all deposited material remelts each cycle","Materials are constrained by switching and stability together","Optimizing crystallization speed while ignoring amorphous retention"],"answer":1,"explanation":"材料選擇同時受切換與穩定性約束；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Materials are constrained by switching and stability together. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-11"],"title":"材料組成：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Material composition: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只追求最快結晶而忽略非晶保持」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Optimizing crystallization speed while ignoring amorphous retention.","instruction":"接續前一步「材料組成」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只追求最快結晶而忽略非晶保持」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：材料偏析可能累積造成失效。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Material composition artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Optimizing crystallization speed while ignoring amorphous retention\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Segregation can accumulate into failure. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"材料選擇同時受切換與穩定性約束；材料偏析可能累積造成失效。","observationEn":"Materials are constrained by switching and stability together; Segregation can accumulate into failure.","failure":"若採用「只追求最快結晶而忽略非晶保持」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Optimizing crystallization speed while ignoring amorphous retention\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「材料組成」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「材料偏析可能累積造成失效」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Material composition, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Segregation can accumulate into failure\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-12-k1","title":"材料組成／物理與模型","titleEn":"Material composition / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：材料偏析可能累積造成失效。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Segregation can accumulate into failure."},{"id":"a074-v8-12-k2","title":"材料組成／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Material composition / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只追求最快結晶而忽略非晶保持」與「材料選擇同時受切換與穩定性約束」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Optimizing crystallization speed while ignoring amorphous retention\" is not equivalent to \"Materials are constrained by switching and stability together\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「材料組成」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Material composition?","options":["只追求最快結晶而忽略非晶保持","把全部沉積材料當成每次都重熔","材料偏析可能累積造成失效"],"optionsEn":["Optimizing crystallization speed while ignoring amorphous retention","Assuming all deposited material remelts each cycle","Segregation can accumulate into failure"],"answer":2,"explanation":"材料偏析可能累積造成失效；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Segregation can accumulate into failure. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a074-stage03","order":3,"title":"受限相變體積 → 多位準","titleEn":"Confined active volume to Multilevel states","description":"把「受限相變體積」「電阻漂移」「多位準」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Confined active volume, Resistance drift, Multilevel states.","steps":[{"id":"a074-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-12"],"title":"受限相變體積：建立模型","titleEn":"Confined active volume: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「外圍材料未必每次都完成相變」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Surrounding material need not transform each cycle.","instruction":"畫蘑菇型與受限結構的熱區，將有效區和外圍材料分色。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw mushroom/confined thermal regions and separate active from surrounding material. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"外圍材料未必每次都完成相變；有效熱區可小於電極覆蓋面積。","observationEn":"Surrounding material need not transform each cycle; Active thermal volume can be smaller than electrode area.","failure":"若採用「把全部沉積材料當成每次都重熔」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming all deposited material remelts each cycle\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「受限相變體積」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：外圍材料未必每次都完成相變。","checkEn":"Submit the Confined active volume diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Surrounding material need not transform each cycle.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-13-k1","title":"受限相變體積／物理與模型","titleEn":"Confined active volume / Physics and model","text":"機制：外圍材料未必每次都完成相變。","textEn":"Mechanism: Surrounding material need not transform each cycle."},{"id":"a074-v8-13-k2","title":"受限相變體積／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Confined active volume / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把全部沉積材料當成每次都重熔」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming all deposited material remelts each cycle."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「受限相變體積」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Confined active volume, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["外圍材料未必每次都完成相變","把全部沉積材料當成每次都重熔","用不同延遲電阻比較寫入一致性"],"optionsEn":["Surrounding material need not transform each cycle","Assuming all deposited material remelts each cycle","Comparing write consistency at different read delays"],"answer":0,"explanation":"外圍材料未必每次都完成相變；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Surrounding material need not transform each cycle. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-13"],"title":"受限相變體積：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Confined active volume: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把全部沉積材料當成每次都重熔」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming all deposited material remelts each cycle.","instruction":"接續前一步「受限相變體積」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把全部沉積材料當成每次都重熔」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：有效熱區可小於電極覆蓋面積。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Confined active volume artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming all deposited material remelts each cycle\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Active thermal volume can be smaller than electrode area. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"外圍材料未必每次都完成相變；有效熱區可小於電極覆蓋面積。","observationEn":"Surrounding material need not transform each cycle; Active thermal volume can be smaller than electrode area.","failure":"若採用「把全部沉積材料當成每次都重熔」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming all deposited material remelts each cycle\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「受限相變體積」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「有效熱區可小於電極覆蓋面積」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Confined active volume, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Active thermal volume can be smaller than electrode area\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-14-k1","title":"受限相變體積／物理與模型","titleEn":"Confined active volume / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：有效熱區可小於電極覆蓋面積。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Active thermal volume can be smaller than electrode area."},{"id":"a074-v8-14-k2","title":"受限相變體積／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Confined active volume / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把全部沉積材料當成每次都重熔」與「外圍材料未必每次都完成相變」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming all deposited material remelts each cycle\" is not equivalent to \"Surrounding material need not transform each cycle\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「受限相變體積」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Confined active volume?","options":["用不同延遲電阻比較寫入一致性","有效熱區可小於電極覆蓋面積","把全部沉積材料當成每次都重熔"],"optionsEn":["Comparing write consistency at different read delays","Active thermal volume can be smaller than electrode area","Assuming all deposited material remelts each cycle"],"answer":1,"explanation":"有效熱區可小於電極覆蓋面積；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Active thermal volume can be smaller than electrode area. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-14"],"title":"電阻漂移：建立模型","titleEn":"Resistance drift: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「讀取時間不同會影響相同初態的電阻」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Read timing affects resistance even for identical initial states.","instruction":"用自訂 R=R0(t/t0)^ν 比較兩個 ν，標明模型及時間窗。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare two hypothetical drift exponents using R=R0(t/t0)^ν with a time window. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"讀取時間不同會影響相同初態的電阻；漂移參數依溫度和初始態而變。","observationEn":"Read timing affects resistance even for identical initial states; Drift depends on temperature and initial state.","failure":"若採用「用不同延遲電阻比較寫入一致性」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Comparing write consistency at different read delays\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「電阻漂移」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：讀取時間不同會影響相同初態的電阻。","checkEn":"Submit the Resistance drift diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Read timing affects resistance even for identical initial states.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-15-k1","title":"電阻漂移／物理與模型","titleEn":"Resistance drift / Physics and model","text":"機制：讀取時間不同會影響相同初態的電阻。","textEn":"Mechanism: Read timing affects resistance even for identical initial states."},{"id":"a074-v8-15-k2","title":"電阻漂移／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Resistance drift / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「用不同延遲電阻比較寫入一致性」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Comparing write consistency at different read delays."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電阻漂移」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Resistance drift, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["用不同延遲電阻比較寫入一致性","初始分開就保證長期不重疊","讀取時間不同會影響相同初態的電阻"],"optionsEn":["Comparing write consistency at different read delays","Assuming initial separation guarantees permanent separation","Read timing affects resistance even for identical initial states"],"answer":2,"explanation":"讀取時間不同會影響相同初態的電阻；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Read timing affects resistance even for identical initial states. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-15"],"title":"電阻漂移：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Resistance drift: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「用不同延遲電阻比較寫入一致性」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Comparing write consistency at different read delays.","instruction":"接續前一步「電阻漂移」成果，先指出錯誤主張「用不同延遲電阻比較寫入一致性」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：漂移參數依溫度和初始態而變。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Resistance drift artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Comparing write consistency at different read delays\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Drift depends on temperature and initial state. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"讀取時間不同會影響相同初態的電阻；漂移參數依溫度和初始態而變。","observationEn":"Read timing affects resistance even for identical initial states; Drift depends on temperature and initial state.","failure":"若採用「用不同延遲電阻比較寫入一致性」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Comparing write consistency at different read delays\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「電阻漂移」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「漂移參數依溫度和初始態而變」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Resistance drift, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Drift depends on temperature and initial state\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-16-k1","title":"電阻漂移／物理與模型","titleEn":"Resistance drift / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：漂移參數依溫度和初始態而變。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Drift depends on temperature and initial state."},{"id":"a074-v8-16-k2","title":"電阻漂移／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Resistance drift / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「用不同延遲電阻比較寫入一致性」與「讀取時間不同會影響相同初態的電阻」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Comparing write consistency at different read delays\" is not equivalent to \"Read timing affects resistance even for identical initial states\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「電阻漂移」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Resistance drift?","options":["漂移參數依溫度和初始態而變","用不同延遲電阻比較寫入一致性","初始分開就保證長期不重疊"],"optionsEn":["Drift depends on temperature and initial state","Comparing write consistency at different read delays","Assuming initial separation guarantees permanent separation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"漂移參數依溫度和初始態而變；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Drift depends on temperature and initial state. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-16"],"title":"多位準：建立模型","titleEn":"Multilevel states: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「可分辨狀態數受漂移與變異共同限制」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Distinguishable states are limited by drift and variability.","instruction":"畫部分結晶的三個假設電阻窗，加入漂移和讀取雜訊。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw three partial-crystallization windows including drift and read noise. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"可分辨狀態數受漂移與變異共同限制；狀態間相鄰重疊需看分布尾端。","observationEn":"Distinguishable states are limited by drift and variability; Neighbor-state overlap requires tail analysis.","failure":"若採用「初始分開就保證長期不重疊」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming initial separation guarantees permanent separation\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「多位準」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：可分辨狀態數受漂移與變異共同限制。","checkEn":"Submit the Multilevel states diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Distinguishable states are limited by drift and variability.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-17-k1","title":"多位準／物理與模型","titleEn":"Multilevel states / Physics and model","text":"機制：可分辨狀態數受漂移與變異共同限制。","textEn":"Mechanism: Distinguishable states are limited by drift and variability."},{"id":"a074-v8-17-k2","title":"多位準／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Multilevel states / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「初始分開就保證長期不重疊」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming initial separation guarantees permanent separation."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「多位準」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Multilevel states, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["將 OTS 閾值切換直接等同 PCM 相變","可分辨狀態數受漂移與變異共同限制","初始分開就保證長期不重疊"],"optionsEn":["Equating OTS threshold switching directly with PCM phase change","Distinguishable states are limited by drift and variability","Assuming initial separation guarantees permanent separation"],"answer":1,"explanation":"可分辨狀態數受漂移與變異共同限制；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Distinguishable states are limited by drift and variability. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-17"],"title":"多位準：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Multilevel states: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「初始分開就保證長期不重疊」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming initial separation guarantees permanent separation.","instruction":"接續前一步「多位準」成果，先指出錯誤主張「初始分開就保證長期不重疊」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：狀態間相鄰重疊需看分布尾端。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Multilevel states artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming initial separation guarantees permanent separation\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Neighbor-state overlap requires tail analysis. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"可分辨狀態數受漂移與變異共同限制；狀態間相鄰重疊需看分布尾端。","observationEn":"Distinguishable states are limited by drift and variability; Neighbor-state overlap requires tail analysis.","failure":"若採用「初始分開就保證長期不重疊」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming initial separation guarantees permanent separation\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「多位準」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「狀態間相鄰重疊需看分布尾端」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Multilevel states, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Neighbor-state overlap requires tail analysis\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-18-k1","title":"多位準／物理與模型","titleEn":"Multilevel states / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：狀態間相鄰重疊需看分布尾端。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Neighbor-state overlap requires tail analysis."},{"id":"a074-v8-18-k2","title":"多位準／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Multilevel states / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「初始分開就保證長期不重疊」與「可分辨狀態數受漂移與變異共同限制」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming initial separation guarantees permanent separation\" is not equivalent to \"Distinguishable states are limited by drift and variability\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「多位準」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Multilevel states?","options":["初始分開就保證長期不重疊","將 OTS 閾值切換直接等同 PCM 相變","狀態間相鄰重疊需看分布尾端"],"optionsEn":["Assuming initial separation guarantees permanent separation","Equating OTS threshold switching directly with PCM phase change","Neighbor-state overlap requires tail analysis"],"answer":2,"explanation":"狀態間相鄰重疊需看分布尾端；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Neighbor-state overlap requires tail analysis. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a074-stage04","order":4,"title":"選擇器與偷流 → 陣列耐久度","titleEn":"Selector and sneak paths to Array endurance","description":"把「選擇器與偷流」「過度編程」「陣列耐久度」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Selector and sneak paths, Over-programming, Array endurance.","steps":[{"id":"a074-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-18"],"title":"選擇器與偷流：建立模型","titleEn":"Selector and sneak paths: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「選擇器與記憶材料的職責不同」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Selectors and storage material serve different roles.","instruction":"畫一個交叉點陣列，追蹤選中路徑與未選中旁路。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw a cross-point array and trace selected and sneak paths. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"選擇器與記憶材料的職責不同；選擇器導通壓降消耗部分寫入能量。","observationEn":"Selectors and storage material serve different roles; Selector voltage drop consumes write energy.","failure":"若採用「將 OTS 閾值切換直接等同 PCM 相變」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating OTS threshold switching directly with PCM phase change\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「選擇器與偷流」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：選擇器與記憶材料的職責不同。","checkEn":"Submit the Selector and sneak paths diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Selectors and storage material serve different roles.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-19-k1","title":"選擇器與偷流／物理與模型","titleEn":"Selector and sneak paths / Physics and model","text":"機制：選擇器與記憶材料的職責不同。","textEn":"Mechanism: Selectors and storage material serve different roles."},{"id":"a074-v8-19-k2","title":"選擇器與偷流／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Selector and sneak paths / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「將 OTS 閾值切換直接等同 PCM 相變」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating OTS threshold switching directly with PCM phase change."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「選擇器與偷流」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Selector and sneak paths, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["選擇器與記憶材料的職責不同","將 OTS 閾值切換直接等同 PCM 相變","高阻態越高就一定壽命越長"],"optionsEn":["Selectors and storage material serve different roles","Equating OTS threshold switching directly with PCM phase change","Assuming higher RESET resistance guarantees longer life"],"answer":0,"explanation":"選擇器與記憶材料的職責不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Selectors and storage material serve different roles. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-19"],"title":"選擇器與偷流：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Selector and sneak paths: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「將 OTS 閾值切換直接等同 PCM 相變」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating OTS threshold switching directly with PCM phase change.","instruction":"接續前一步「選擇器與偷流」成果，先指出錯誤主張「將 OTS 閾值切換直接等同 PCM 相變」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：選擇器導通壓降消耗部分寫入能量。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Selector and sneak paths artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating OTS threshold switching directly with PCM phase change\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Selector voltage drop consumes write energy. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"選擇器與記憶材料的職責不同；選擇器導通壓降消耗部分寫入能量。","observationEn":"Selectors and storage material serve different roles; Selector voltage drop consumes write energy.","failure":"若採用「將 OTS 閾值切換直接等同 PCM 相變」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating OTS threshold switching directly with PCM phase change\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「選擇器與偷流」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「選擇器導通壓降消耗部分寫入能量」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Selector and sneak paths, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Selector voltage drop consumes write energy\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-20-k1","title":"選擇器與偷流／物理與模型","titleEn":"Selector and sneak paths / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：選擇器導通壓降消耗部分寫入能量。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Selector voltage drop consumes write energy."},{"id":"a074-v8-20-k2","title":"選擇器與偷流／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Selector and sneak paths / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「將 OTS 閾值切換直接等同 PCM 相變」與「選擇器與記憶材料的職責不同」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating OTS threshold switching directly with PCM phase change\" is not equivalent to \"Selectors and storage material serve different roles\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「選擇器與偷流」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Selector and sneak paths?","options":["高阻態越高就一定壽命越長","選擇器導通壓降消耗部分寫入能量","將 OTS 閾值切換直接等同 PCM 相變"],"optionsEn":["Assuming higher RESET resistance guarantees longer life","Selector voltage drop consumes write energy","Equating OTS threshold switching directly with PCM phase change"],"answer":1,"explanation":"選擇器導通壓降消耗部分寫入能量；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Selector voltage drop consumes write energy. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-20"],"title":"過度編程：建立模型","titleEn":"Over-programming: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「更大寫入能量可能加速材料劣化」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Greater write energy can accelerate material degradation.","instruction":"比較達標即停與過強 RESET 的假設循環圖，列出偏析證據。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare stop-on-target and excessive RESET cycling and specify segregation evidence. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"更大寫入能量可能加速材料劣化；更短脈衝未必有較低總能量。","observationEn":"Greater write energy can accelerate material degradation; Shorter pulses need not have lower total energy.","failure":"若採用「高阻態越高就一定壽命越長」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming higher RESET resistance guarantees longer life\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「過度編程」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：更大寫入能量可能加速材料劣化。","checkEn":"Submit the Over-programming diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Greater write energy can accelerate material degradation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-21-k1","title":"過度編程／物理與模型","titleEn":"Over-programming / Physics and model","text":"機制：更大寫入能量可能加速材料劣化。","textEn":"Mechanism: Greater write energy can accelerate material degradation."},{"id":"a074-v8-21-k2","title":"過度編程／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Over-programming / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「高阻態越高就一定壽命越長」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming higher RESET resistance guarantees longer life."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「過度編程」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Over-programming, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["高阻態越高就一定壽命越長","挑最佳單元的次數代表所有位元","更大寫入能量可能加速材料劣化"],"optionsEn":["Assuming higher RESET resistance guarantees longer life","Using the best cell's cycle count for every bit","Greater write energy can accelerate material degradation"],"answer":2,"explanation":"更大寫入能量可能加速材料劣化；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Greater write energy can accelerate material degradation. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-21"],"title":"過度編程：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Over-programming: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「高阻態越高就一定壽命越長」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming higher RESET resistance guarantees longer life.","instruction":"接續前一步「過度編程」成果，先指出錯誤主張「高阻態越高就一定壽命越長」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：更短脈衝未必有較低總能量。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Over-programming artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming higher RESET resistance guarantees longer life\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Shorter pulses need not have lower total energy. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"更大寫入能量可能加速材料劣化；更短脈衝未必有較低總能量。","observationEn":"Greater write energy can accelerate material degradation; Shorter pulses need not have lower total energy.","failure":"若採用「高阻態越高就一定壽命越長」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming higher RESET resistance guarantees longer life\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「過度編程」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「更短脈衝未必有較低總能量」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Over-programming, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Shorter pulses need not have lower total energy\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-22-k1","title":"過度編程／物理與模型","titleEn":"Over-programming / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：更短脈衝未必有較低總能量。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Shorter pulses need not have lower total energy."},{"id":"a074-v8-22-k2","title":"過度編程／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Over-programming / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「高阻態越高就一定壽命越長」與「更大寫入能量可能加速材料劣化」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming higher RESET resistance guarantees longer life\" is not equivalent to \"Greater write energy can accelerate material degradation\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「過度編程」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Over-programming?","options":["更短脈衝未必有較低總能量","高阻態越高就一定壽命越長","挑最佳單元的次數代表所有位元"],"optionsEn":["Shorter pulses need not have lower total energy","Assuming higher RESET resistance guarantees longer life","Using the best cell's cycle count for every bit"],"answer":0,"explanation":"更短脈衝未必有較低總能量；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Shorter pulses need not have lower total energy. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-22"],"title":"陣列耐久度：建立模型","titleEn":"Array endurance: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「單元展示和整陣列可靠度證據不同」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Single-cell demonstrations and array reliability are different evidence.","instruction":"將平均值、早失效尾端和測試中未失效樣本同時報告。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Report means, early-failure tails and surviving array cells together. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"單元展示和整陣列可靠度證據不同；耐久與保持通常需不同測試序列。","observationEn":"Single-cell demonstrations and array reliability are different evidence; Endurance and retention need different test sequences.","failure":"若採用「挑最佳單元的次數代表所有位元」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using the best cell's cycle count for every bit\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「陣列耐久度」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：單元展示和整陣列可靠度證據不同。","checkEn":"Submit the Array endurance diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Single-cell demonstrations and array reliability are different evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-23-k1","title":"陣列耐久度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Array endurance / Physics and model","text":"機制：單元展示和整陣列可靠度證據不同。","textEn":"Mechanism: Single-cell demonstrations and array reliability are different evidence."},{"id":"a074-v8-23-k2","title":"陣列耐久度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Array endurance / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「挑最佳單元的次數代表所有位元」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using the best cell's cycle count for every bit."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「陣列耐久度」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Array endurance, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把高阻態都視為燒斷導線","單元展示和整陣列可靠度證據不同","挑最佳單元的次數代表所有位元"],"optionsEn":["Treating every high-resistance state as a burnt wire","Single-cell demonstrations and array reliability are different evidence","Using the best cell's cycle count for every bit"],"answer":1,"explanation":"單元展示和整陣列可靠度證據不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Single-cell demonstrations and array reliability are different evidence. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-23"],"title":"陣列耐久度：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Array endurance: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「挑最佳單元的次數代表所有位元」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using the best cell's cycle count for every bit.","instruction":"接續前一步「陣列耐久度」成果，先指出錯誤主張「挑最佳單元的次數代表所有位元」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：耐久與保持通常需不同測試序列。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Array endurance artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using the best cell's cycle count for every bit\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Endurance and retention need different test sequences. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"單元展示和整陣列可靠度證據不同；耐久與保持通常需不同測試序列。","observationEn":"Single-cell demonstrations and array reliability are different evidence; Endurance and retention need different test sequences.","failure":"若採用「挑最佳單元的次數代表所有位元」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using the best cell's cycle count for every bit\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「陣列耐久度」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「耐久與保持通常需不同測試序列」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Array endurance, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Endurance and retention need different test sequences\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-24-k1","title":"陣列耐久度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Array endurance / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：耐久與保持通常需不同測試序列。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Endurance and retention need different test sequences."},{"id":"a074-v8-24-k2","title":"陣列耐久度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Array endurance / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「挑最佳單元的次數代表所有位元」與「單元展示和整陣列可靠度證據不同」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using the best cell's cycle count for every bit\" is not equivalent to \"Single-cell demonstrations and array reliability are different evidence\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「陣列耐久度」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Array endurance?","options":["挑最佳單元的次數代表所有位元","把高阻態都視為燒斷導線","耐久與保持通常需不同測試序列"],"optionsEn":["Using the best cell's cycle count for every bit","Treating every high-resistance state as a burnt wire","Endurance and retention need different test sequences"],"answer":2,"explanation":"耐久與保持通常需不同測試序列；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Endurance and retention need different test sequences. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"memory","subcategoryTitle":"記憶體","subcategoryTitleEn":"Memory"}};
